From: nwrt Xiaomi 14 Pro integration
Subject: [PATCH] qcom-soc: keep the phone modem operating mode online

The shennong modem remote processor is already online when ModemManager
discovers it.  Sending the generic DMS Set Operating Mode request makes the
phone modem disappear from QRTR and re-enumerate; netifd then receives
MM_INTERFACE_RESTART and can never move the modem past the disabled state.

The embedded phone modem is powered and stopped by the platform remoteproc
lifecycle, not by ModemManager.  Treat DMS operating-mode requests as
successful no-ops only for qcom-soc with Xiaomi's rmnet_ipa0 parent.  Bearer
disconnect and WDS session handling remain active, while generic QMI devices
retain the upstream DMS behaviour.

--- a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
@@ -2566,6 +2566,17 @@ common_power_up_down_off (MMIfaceModem        *_self,
     task = g_task_new (self, NULL, callback, user_data);
 
+    /* The phone modem is already online and is owned by remoteproc.  Sending
+     * DMS Set Operating Mode makes Xiaomi's QRTR services re-enumerate. */
+    if (g_strcmp0 (mm_base_modem_get_plugin (MM_BASE_MODEM (self)), "qcom-soc") == 0 &&
+        g_file_test ("/sys/class/net/rmnet_ipa0", G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS)) {
+        mm_obj_msg (self, "ignoring DMS operating-mode change %u on embedded Xiaomi modem",
+                    (guint) mode);
+        g_task_return_boolean (task, TRUE);
+        g_object_unref (task);
+        return;
+    }
+
     if (self->priv->set_operating_mode_task) {
         error = g_error_new (MM_CORE_ERROR, MM_CORE_ERROR_IN_PROGRESS, "Another operation in progress");
         g_task_return_error (task, error);
